What:		/proc/sentry_remote_reporter/cna
Date:		March 2025
Contact:	Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd. <sxt1001@huawei.com>
Description:
		Configure and display the local CNA for remote event reporting.

		Write Format:
			<unsigned integer> - CNA value in range [0, 16777215]

		Read Format:
			<unsigned integer> - Current CNA value

		Examples:
			# Set CNA to 100
			echo "100" > /proc/sentry_remote_reporter/cna

			# Read current CNA
			cat /proc/sentry_remote_reporter/cna
			100

		Notes:
		- Setting CNA automatically registers UVB CIS function for panic calls
		- Maximum value: 16777215

What:		/proc/sentry_remote_reporter/eid
Date:		March 2025
Contact:	Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd. <sxt1001@huawei.com>
Description:
		Configure and display local EID for URMA communication.

		Write Format:
			"eid1;eid2;..." - Multiple EIDs separated by semicolons

		Read Format:
			"eid1;eid2;..." - Same format as write

		Examples:
			# Set EIDs for multiple dies
			echo "2001:0db8:85a3:0000:0000:8a2e:0370:7334;2001:0db8:85a3:0000:0000: \
			8a2e:0370:7335" > /proc/sentry_remote_reporter/eid

			# Read current EIDs
			cat /proc/sentry_remote_reporter/eid
			2001:0db8:85a3:0000:0000:8a2e:0370:7334;2001:0db8:85a3:0000:0000:8a2e:0370:7335

		Notes:
		- EIDs must use full IPv6 format: 128-bit numbers separated every 4 bits by colons
		- Supports multiple EIDs for multi-die systems
		- Automatically initializes URMA resources when EIDs are set

What:		/proc/sentry_remote_reporter/panic_timeout
Date:		March 2025
Contact:	Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd. <sxt1001@huawei.com>
Description:
		Configure and display timeout value (in milliseconds) for panic event reporting.

		Write Format:
			<unsigned long> - Timeout in milliseconds, range [0, 3600000]

		Read Format:
			<unsigned long> - Current timeout value

		Examples:
			# Set panic timeout to 35000 ms
			echo "35000" > /proc/sentry_remote_reporter/panic_timeout

			# Read current panic timeout
			cat /proc/sentry_remote_reporter/panic_timeout
			35000

		Notes:
		- Default value: 35000 ms
		- Range: 0 to 3600000 ms (1 hour)

